WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:08.760
NARRATOR: Human beings have
always generated garbage.

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:10.830
In the battle to keep
the streets clean,

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:14.040
the mechanized garbage
truck is a combat vehicle.

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:16.110
It crushes tons
of trash en route

00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:18.810
to deliver it to
landfills, incinerators,

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:20.640
and recycling facilities.

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:23.430
Without it, we'd all be
knee deep in garbage.

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:31.580
Garbage trucks have different
approaches to handling garbage.

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:34.655
Some load from the front,
others from the rear or side.

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:37.940
And some are
entirely mechanized,

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:40.190
like this side-loader truck.

00:00:40.190 --> 00:00:44.150
The operator inside the cab
barely needs to lift a finger,

00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:47.960
as the hydraulic lift arm
does all the heavy work.

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:50.390
The garbage truck has
come a long way since it

00:00:50.390 --> 00:00:52.940
hit the street in 1952.

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:54.950
Production on a modern
side-loader truck

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:57.500
begins with the welding robot.

00:00:57.500 --> 00:00:59.990
The robot fuses
numerous steel supports

00:00:59.990 --> 00:01:01.700
to the truck-body floor.

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:03.620
These supports will
allow the truck

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:05.930
to hold up to the
force of tons of trash

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:07.235
being compacted inside.

00:01:08.810 --> 00:01:12.770
Meanwhile, down the line, other
parts, like the roof and sides,

00:01:12.770 --> 00:01:15.110
take shape in
separate assemblies.

00:01:15.110 --> 00:01:17.120
Once they're
complete, they hoist

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:19.910
the large steel parts
into place and assemble

00:01:19.910 --> 00:01:21.860
them within a metal framework.

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:24.500
The framework serves as
a guide to piece together

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:26.990
all the parts of the truck box.

00:01:26.990 --> 00:01:29.180
Once assembled,
the workers clamp

00:01:29.180 --> 00:01:31.490
the parts together to
secure the assembly

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:32.460
as they weld the seams.

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:38.180
The garbage truck body is then
ready for the mechanized parts,

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:39.800
beginning with the hopper.

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:42.890
It's equipped with a
powerful hydraulic compactor

00:01:42.890 --> 00:01:46.460
to squeeze as much trash
as possible into the truck.

00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:49.610
They fit the hopper snugly to
the front of the truck body

00:01:49.610 --> 00:01:50.630
and weld it to it.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:54.950
Then they lift the
tailgate into position

00:01:54.950 --> 00:01:56.150
at the rear of the truck box.

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:02.180
They hinge it to the truck
by sliding heavy-duty steel

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:03.290
pins through brackets.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:09.530
Once hinged, the
tailgate can swing

00:02:09.530 --> 00:02:13.980
up and out of the way to allow
garbage to be discharged.

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:17.450
The driving force for this is
a pair of hydraulic cylinders

00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:20.240
attached by brackets
welded to the tailgate

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:22.640
at one end and the
truck body at the other.

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:28.040
With that job done,
these cylinders

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:30.080
can now extend to
lift the tailgate

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:31.580
and retract to close it.

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:36.050
Across the factory floor,
another team assembles

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:38.270
a pair of steel lift arms.

00:02:38.270 --> 00:02:40.490
These lift arms are
designed for another kind

00:02:40.490 --> 00:02:43.040
of truck, the frontend loader.

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:45.750
It's mainly used to collect
hefty commercial garbage

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:46.550
containers.

00:02:49.070 --> 00:02:52.460
In action, these arms
pivot around the truck cab

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:55.880
and extend to the front to
fork up the trash container

00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:58.700
and deposit the
contents in the hopper.

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:02.210
Hydraulic cylinders also
power these lift arms.

00:03:02.210 --> 00:03:05.510
When the task is complete, the
forks at the end of the arms

00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:07.040
fold back out of the way.

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:13.550
Nearby, workers test this
rear-loader garbage truck.

00:03:13.550 --> 00:03:17.510
Its tailgate is split into two
hoppers, one for recyclables

00:03:17.510 --> 00:03:19.610
and the other for trash.

00:03:19.610 --> 00:03:23.420
Hydraulic systems lift them one
at a time or simultaneously.

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:27.080
Collecting garbage
and disposing of it

00:03:27.080 --> 00:03:29.330
can be tough on a
truck's paint job.

00:03:29.330 --> 00:03:31.415
So they apply an
extra durable finish.

00:03:32.630 --> 00:03:36.170
They spray sealer on the
sanded outer surface followed

00:03:36.170 --> 00:03:38.690
by two coats of epoxy paint.

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:40.445
After that, they
bake on the layers.

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:45.950
Meanwhile, the truck chassis has
arrived from another factory.

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:47.510
It's a standard size.

00:03:47.510 --> 00:03:51.950
So they chop a piece off to size
it for the garbage truck body.

00:03:51.950 --> 00:03:54.320
They install bracket
plates at the back

00:03:54.320 --> 00:03:56.480
and slide thick pins
through the holes

00:03:56.480 --> 00:03:58.175
to join the truck
body to the chassis.

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:05.120
Using a crane, they lift the
automated side loader truck

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:06.755
body onto the modified chassis.

00:04:14.930 --> 00:04:18.170
Once it's installed,
they test the compactor.

00:04:18.170 --> 00:04:20.690
Dual hydraulic cylinders
push the ejector

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:22.340
blade to the back of the truck.

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:27.650
They test the tailgate,
which has, by now,

00:04:27.650 --> 00:04:29.900
but equipped with the
signal lights, mud flaps,

00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:33.425
and other parts, and verify that
everything functions properly.

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:40.550
Once a truck passes muster,
it's ready to handle whatever

00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:42.740
garbage society throws its way.

00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:51.350
And with these automated
garbage trucks,

00:04:51.350 --> 00:04:54.440
there's no need for anyone
to strain their back

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:56.090
or get their hands dirty.

00:04:56.090 --> 00:04:58.640
Because these robot
arms can handle it.

00:04:58.640 --> 00:05:01.390
[MUSIC PLAYING]

